<control>{"schema":"stage-control-v1","digest":"Dynamic terminal summaries overwrite failed and interrupted outcomes with controller-derived or completion-labelled statuses.","lens":"terminal-semantics","findings":[{"severity":"high","title":"Preserve failed and interrupted outcomes before applying dynamic status overrides","file":"src/workflow-terminal.ts","locations":[{"file":"src/workflow-terminal.ts","line":80,"lineEnd":95,"symbol":"summarizeWorkflowTerminal"},{"file":"src/workflow-terminal.ts","line":48,"lineEnd":61,"symbol":"readDynamicControllerControl"},{"file":"src/workflow-terminal.ts","line":64,"lineEnd":69,"symbol":"nonDynamicSemanticStatus"},{"file":"src/workflow-terminal.ts","line":98,"lineEnd":102,"symbol":"summarizeWorkflowTerminal"}],"evidence":"The dynamic override checks terminal status but never requires successful completion. Every branch replaces the semanticStatus initialized from run.status. Without a dynamic_incomplete marker, a failed or interrupted terminal run with missing controller output becomes completed_without_semantic_result; a synthesized controller artifact instead makes it synthesized. Missing controllers and control-file read failures explicitly return undefined, making the fallback reachable without any successful controller result.","evidenceQuotes":["\treturn run.status;","\tif (!controller) return undefined;","\t).catch(() => undefined);","\tif (terminal && run.provenance?.mode === \"direct-dynamic\") {","\t\telse if (control?.status === \"synthesized\") semanticStatus = \"synthesized\";","\t\telse semanticStatus = \"completed_without_semantic_result\";","\t\tengineStatus: run.status,"],"rationale":"Cancellation before controller output exists and failures with unavailable controller artifacts lose their failed/interrupted semantic outcome. An existing synthesized artifact can also override those outcomes because controller success and artifact currency are not checked here. Although engineStatus remains accurate, consumers